Input: {"question": "What year was Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus elected consul?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d00", "start": 0, "end": 151, "text": "Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC) Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus was the son of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus, consul in 148 BC."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d00", "start": 152, "end": 203, "text": "He was consul in 112 BC, with Marcus Livius Drusus."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d00", "start": 204, "end": 485, "text": "In 107 BC, he served as legate to the consul, Lucius Cassius Longinus, who was sent into Gaul to oppose the Cimbri and their allies, and he fell together with the consul in the battle, in which the Roman army was utterly defeated by the Tigurini in the territory of the Allobroges."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d00", "start": 486, "end": 589, "text": "This Piso was the grandfather of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus, the father-in-law of Julius Caesar,"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 0, "end": 40, "text": "Geschlecht der Calpurnier und war 112 v."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 41, "end": 46, "text": "Chr ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 47, "end": 55, "text": "Konsul ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 56, "end": 127, "text": "( de ) Lucio Calpurnio Pisón Cesonino ( en latín , Lucius Calpurnius L."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 128, "end": 130, "text": "F."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 131, "end": 133, "text": "C."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 134, "end": 136, "text": "N."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 137, "end": 205, "text": "Piso Caesoninus ) fue un político y militar de la República Romana ."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 206, "end": 275, "text": "Era hijo de Lucio Calpurnio Pisón Cesonino , que fue cónsul en 148 a."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 276, "end": 278, "text": "C."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 279, "end": 389, "text": "( es ) Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus was the son of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus , consul in 148 BC ."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 390, "end": 443, "text": "He was consul in 112 BC , with Marcus Livius Drusus ."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d01", "start": 444, "end": 489, "text": "In 107 BC , he served as legate to the consul"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d02", "start": 0, "end": 492, "text": "Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus ( consul 112 BC ) - Wikiwand English Sign in Top Qs Timeline Chat Perspective AI tools Top Qs Timeline Chat Perspective All Articles Dictionary Quotes Map Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus ( consul 112 BC ) Roman General and Consul From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus ( consul 112 BC ) Family References For other people named Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus , see Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus ( disambiguation ) ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d02", "start": 493, "end": 596, "text": "Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus was the son of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus , consul in 148 BC ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d02", "start": 597, "end": 615, "text": "This article needs"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d03", "start": 0, "end": 128, "text": "Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 148 BC) Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus was a Roman statesman in the 2nd century BC."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d03", "start": 129, "end": 222, "text": "He was elected consul in the year 148 BC, serving alongside Spurius Postumius Albinus Magnus."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d03", "start": 223, "end": 333, "text": "His last name indicates that he was originally a member of the Caesonia and was adopted by one of the Pisones."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d03", "start": 334, "end": 499, "text": "Lucius served as Praetor in 154 BC, receiving the province Hispania Ulterior during the period of the Lusitanian War; he was defeated in battle against the Lusitani."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d03", "start": 500, "end": 598, "text": "He was consul during the second year of the Third Punic War, which he conducted so lackadaisically"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d04", "start": 0, "end": 51, "text": "that Caesar conquered the year of Piso's consulate."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d04", "start": 52, "end": 349, "text": "As Caesar's father-in-law, when Cicero was faced with exile later that year for having violated the \"Leges Clodiae\" by executing members of the Cataline conspiracy without a formal trial, Piso declined to protect Cicero from the threat and consequences of exile, earning the enmity of that orator."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d04", "start": 350, "end": 581, "text": "In response, Cicero attacked Piso both during and after his subsequent administration of the province of Macedonia, which he administered from 57 BC to the beginning of 55 BC, when he was recalled and replaced by Quintus Ancharius."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d04", "start": 582, "end": 625, "text": "Piso's recall was perhaps in consequence of"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 0, "end": 74, "text": "successes there , the senate honoured him with the ornamenta triumphalia ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 75, "end": 173, "text": "[ 2 ] [ 3 ] Piso may have also been proconsul of Asia and legate of Syria , but this is disputed ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 174, "end": 269, "text": "He was praefectus urbi from AD 13 to 32 , and a trusted adviser to both Augustus and Tiberius ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 270, "end": 339, "text": "He was a member of the pontifical college and of the Arval Brethren ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 340, "end": 395, "text": "He died in 32 , and was honoured with a state funeral ."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 396, "end": 462, "text": "[ 4 ] Piso 's achievements and independence were highly regarded ."}, "D6S7": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d05", "start": 463, "end": 495, "text": "Horace dedicated his Ars Poëtica"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d06", "start": 0, "end": 11, "text": "1993 , pp ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d06", "start": 12, "end": 24, "text": "166 , 167 n."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d06", "start": 25, "end": 34, "text": "1 , 184 ."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb:d06", "start": 35, "end": 57